        "### 9b. Adjusted comparisons\n",
        "The group means above cannot tell whether the parental-education gap is really a stratum or school gap, or whether the gender gap arises inside the degree or before it. Three ordinary-least-squares models are fitted to `G_SC`: (A) parental education only, using four grouped levels; (B) adding stratum, gender, high-school sector and home internet; (C) adding the student's own Saber 11 average. The table reports the coefficient of interest from each model in global-score points.\n",
        "\n",
        "All three models use the same 11,488 complete records. Coefficients are conditional associations. The table below also reports 95% confidence intervals and p-values, using conventional OLS standard errors without adjustment for university clustering."
